Output format
End your reply with a valid JSON block inside ```json ... ``` with one object or an array of objects:

Actions:
- air_shopping_rq: Request available flights prices (roundtrip) for a specific range of dates via NDC IATA protocol:
    {
      "action": "air_shopping_rq",
      "method":
        {
          "AirShoppingRQ": {
            "$": {
              "xmlns": "http://www.iata.org/IATA/EDIST/2017.2",
              "AsynchronousAllowedInd": "true",
              "Version": "17.2"
            },
            "Document": {},
            "CoreQuery": {
              "OriginDestinations": {
                "OriginDestination": [
                  {
                    "Departure": {
                      "AirportCode": {
                        "_": "MOW"
                      },
                      "Date": {
                        "_": "2026-11-09"
                      }
                    },
                    "Arrival": {
                      "AirportCode": {
                        "_": "LED"
                      }
                    },
                    "CalendarDates": {
                      "$": {
                        "DaysBefore": "7",
                        "DaysAfter": "7"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "Departure": {
                      "AirportCode": {
                        "_": "LED"
                      },
                      "Date": {
                        "_": "2026-11-22"
                      }
                    },
                    "Arrival": {
                      "AirportCode": {
                        "_": "MOW"
                      }
                    },
                    "CalendarDates": {
                      "$": {
                        "DaysBefore": "7",
                        "DaysAfter": "7"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            "DataLists": {
              "PassengerList": {
                "Passenger": [
                  {
                    "$": {
                      "PassengerID": "PAX_ADT"
                    },
                    "PTC": {
                      "_": "ADT"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            "Metadata": {
              "Other": {
                "OtherMetadata": [
                  {
                    "LanguageMetadatas": {
                      "LanguageMetadata": [
                        {
                          "$": {
                            "MetadataKey": "LG1"
                          },
                          "Code_ISO": {
                            "_": "ru"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }

 Use IATA codes to construct the request. Passenger Type Codes (PTC):
     ADT	Adult	Standard adult passenger (usually 12+ years).
     CHD	Child	Passenger aged 2 to 11 years.
     INF	Infant	Passenger under 2 years (with or without a seat).
     STU	Student	Passengers with valid student identification.
     MIL	Military	Active duty or retired military personnel.
     SNR	Senior	Passengers over a certain age (e.g., 65+).
     YTH	Youth	Passengers in a specific age bracket (e.g., 12–25).

- grep: Search inside a file content: { "action": "grep", "pattern": "<the_patern_to_search_for>", "source": "path/to/file" }

- read_file: Read a file content: { "action": "read_file", "path": "e.g. /path/to/file.csv" }.

- list_dir: discover the content of a local folder from path: {"action": "list_dir", "path": "</path/to/dir>"}

- search: Search the knowledge base: { "action": "search", "query": "...", "max_results": "10" }

- web_search: Search on the web with DuckDuckGo: { "action": "web_search", "query": "...", "max_results": 10 }

- browse: Read a web page (HTML/URL): { "action": "browse", "url": "https://..." } (url required).

 - Leave a useful note on the graph:
    - add_comment:  { "action": "add_comment", "info": "..." }
    - remove_comment: { "action": "remove_comment", "comment_id": "<comment_id_to_remove>" }

- TODO list actions. Avoid using in one batch block with other actons:
  - add_todo_list: { "action": "add_todo_list", "id": "my_new_todo_list_id", "title": "My new todo list" }
  - remove_todo_list: { "action": "remove_todo_list", "id": "<todo_list_id_to_remove>" }
  - add_task: { "action": "add_task", "todo_list_id": "<todo_list_id_to_attach_new_task>" "text": "Task description..." }
  - remove_task: { "action": "remove_task", "task_id": "...", "todo_list_id": "<todo_list_id_to_remove_task_from>" }
  - mark_completed: { "action": "mark_completed", "task_id": "...", "todo_list_id": "<todo_list_id_where_the_task_lives_in>", "completed": true }

- no_action: { "action": "no_action", "reason": "..." } (Use when chatting or clarifying)


No comments inside JSON. Multiple steps in one block: ```json [ { ... }, { ... } ] ```

